    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27773" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῐώνῠμ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίς, ὄνυμα, ὄνομα</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with two names,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.T.
				636.11
			</span></i> (s. v. l.); or, of two persons, <i>named together,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					683
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διά</span>) <i>far-famed,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐτυχία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Tim.</u>
					30
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρατηγός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					App.
					<u>BC</u>
					4.54
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χῶρος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>BJ</u>
					5.1.3
				</span></i>
			.</div>
